{
  "_comment": "The municipality join (issue #137): one entry per municipal body, and every spelling VRK's pages publish for it as an alias. The parsers pass each era's wording through verbatim -- 'Vilniaus miesto' on the 1997/2000/2002/2019/2023 cards, 'Vilniaus miesto savivaldybė' on 2007/2011/2015, 'Palangos savivaldybė' in 2011 alone -- so without this file every one of the 60 municipalities appeared twice in the dashboard's facet and in the shipped `municipality` column, each half hiding the other half of its history. `name` is the official name of the body; `kind` its type (miesto / rajono / savivaldybe); `aliases` the published forms, matched exactly after whitespace normalisation and the mayoral cards' constituency number ('Telšių rajono (Nr. 51)') is stripped -- scraper/shared/municipalities.py never guesses. The two 1997 Marijampolė bodies stay separate entries with `until`: the 2000 reform merged a city and a district into one new municipality, and a facet that folded them would put a 1997 district councillor under a body that did not exist. docs/municipality-forms.tsv is the measured form table and tests/test_municipality_registry.py holds every form to exactly one entry.",
